<title>FRANCE: Court voids Galeries Lafayette layoff plan.</title>
<headline>Court voids Galeries Lafayette layoff plan.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Paris court declared void a plan drawn up in April by retailer Galeries Lafayette to lay off 344 of its 10,000 workers.</p>
<p>Galeries Lafayette human resources director Gilbert Mero told Reuters the court's decision, announced on Wednesday, criticised the reclassification programme entailed in the plan.</p>
<p>He said the company had not drawn up an alternative plan.</p>
</text>
